+ * Per-handle idempotency:
+ *   Before docker run, acquires: SET dispatch:lock:<handle> <owner> NX PX <ttl>
+ *   Only the lock winner spawns; losers skip + XACK to remove from their PEL.
+ *   The platform.handle=<handle> label check is a cheap post-spawn backstop.
+ *
+ * DLQ handling:
+ *   After maxDeliveries, the entry is moved to DISPATCH_DLQ_KEY and a
+ *   synthetic "failed" completion is posted to the broker /callback, routing
+ *   the terminal failure through the normal completion path.
+ *
+ * Global spawn cap:
+ *   Before spawning, reads broker GET /registry-size and skips if at cap.
+ *   On cap-exceeded, the entry is left pending (XREADGROUP will redeliver).
+ */
